                <pb facs="1084" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg964"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.00 Revolution 1931/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-08T18:00:00+00:00">April 8, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Referring to my telegram No. 4, April 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>], 4
                    p.m., Consul at Funchal has telegraphed Legation that leaders revolutionary
                    forces have agreed to meet representatives Central Government forces to discuss
                    situation and Consul suggests American Consulate as meeting place, requesting
                    Legation to endeavor to arrange as above through Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>I have discussed informally matter with Foreign Minister as to Central
                    Government’s wishes and indicated to him that I would request Department to
                    authorize Consul to lend his good offices to extent he requests.</p>
                <p>Foreign Minister expressed great appreciation and said that he would inform me of
                    his Government’s wishes after a Cabinet meeting tonight and confidentially
                    informed me British Ambassador had made same proposal for British Consul,
                    Funchal, except the meeting place proposed is British cruiser due at Funchal
                    tonight. Will appreciate Department’s rushing instructions to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">South</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
